.TH "HTMLMEDIAELEMENT.ABORT_EVENT" "3JS" "June 5, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLMediaElement.abort_event \- HTMLMediaElement: abort event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]abort\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when media resource
loading is stopped before completion, but not as the result of an error.
This is usually achieved by removing the \f[CR]src\f[R] attribute or
setting it to the empty string (\f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]), then calling
\f[CR]load()\f[R].
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqabort\(dq, (event) => { })

onabort = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Abort loading a media resource
The following example demonstrates how to abort a video.
When you press the button it starts loading a video resource.
After a short timeout it aborts the load by removing the \f[CR]src\f[R]
attribute and calling the \f[CR]load()\f[R] method.
If the video resource is still loading when \f[CR]load()\f[R] is called,
the \f[CR]abort\f[R] event fires.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]video\f[R] controls width=\(dq250\(dq></\f[B]video\f[R]>

<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqloadAndAbort\(dq>Load and abort video</\f[B]button\f[R]>

<\f[B]pre\f[R] id=\(dqlog\(dq></\f[B]pre\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
.IP
.EX
video,
button,
pre {
  \f[B]display\f[R]: block;
  \f[B]margin\-block\f[R]: 1rem;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] video = document.querySelector(\(dqvideo\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] loadAndAbortButton = document.querySelector(\(dq#loadAndAbort\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] log = document.querySelector(\(dq#log\(dq);

video.addEventListener(\(dqabort\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  log.textContent += \(dqVideo loading aborted\(rsn\(dq;
});

loadAndAbortButton.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  log.textContent = \(dqLoading video...\(rsn\(dq;

  video.src = \(ga/shared\-assets/videos/flower.webm?nocache=${Date.now()}\(ga;
  video.load();

  setTimeout(() \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    video.removeAttribute(\(dqsrc\(dq);
    video.load();
  }, 50);
});
.EE
